  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.amc-8-2014-p22.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Let the number be \\(10a+b\\), where \\(a\\) is the tens digit and \\(b\\) is the units digit. The condition gives \\[ab+a+b=10a+b.\\]\n\nCanceling \\(b\\) from both sides gives \\(ab+a=10a\\), so \\(ab=9a\\). Since \\(a\\neq0\\), we get \\(b=9\\).\n\nThus, E is the correct answer.",
      "hints": [
        "Let the tens digit be \\(a\\) and the units digit be \\(b\\).",
        "Translate the condition into \\(ab+a+b=10a+b\\)."
      ],
